the thematics behind the two are quite different, and that is reflected in what the two &quot;staring values&quot; *should* be. A mummy should *not* have a Balance of 1 at the beginning, as that indicates a mummy who only *barely* &quot;passed the test&quot;, as it were, which is really only the case with Udja-Sen; other mummies &quot;should&quot; having ratings somewhere between 3-5 to start, as that would better represent the &quot;completeness&quot; of soul/purpose that they now have via the Completing Spirit. It's most emphatically *not* the same as a newly (A)wakened mage who may only have a dot in Arete (though, again, per the RAW, very few starting mages have only one dot in it, as the initial Awakening often results in a starting Arete of 1-3, per the use of Freebies and as indicated in the Storyteller's Guide/other books).<br /> <br /> M:tR had a number of good ideas, and was an improvement over the previous editions; however, this and a few other things (don't *even* get me started on some of the Purposes, mechanically, or the Udja-Sen, specifically -- we'll be here all day...) were so miscalculated it's a wonder they made it past review/play-testing with a book that was published in the Revised era (that is, unlike with the 1st Ed. books back in the early 90's, there had already been enough years and editions that such meta-conceptual/metaphysical oversights such as these should really have not still been occurring).<br /> <br /> But anywho....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it could be possible to divide balance into balance and a new trait called sekhem. but then... what would balance do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Pos